<h2>Production time versus total project schedule</h2>
<p>An architectural model project has three separate schedule components:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Pre-production and approvals:</strong> Confirming the model boundary, scale, details, materials, colors and source files.</li>
<li><strong>Internal production:</strong> Digital preparation, fabrication, assembly, finishing, quality control, final photography and client final approval.</li>
<li><strong>Delivery:</strong> Polish, clean packing, shipping and any required on-site installation.</li>
</ol>
<p>Carve Model's standard 14–21 day target refers to internal production. Time spent waiting for client comments, revised drawings, material approvals or final authorization is not included in that production period.</p>

